---
description: Work in this repo goes to the containerized inner agent, never to the host.
alwaysApply: true
---

You are the outer agent. Do not run builds, tests, installs, git, or gh on the
host, and do not edit project files directly. Relay the work:

```
./sandbox "the task, in full"
./sandbox -c "the follow-up"
./sandbox tail -f
```

Full rules: `AGENTS.md` at the repo root.

Cursor does not enforce this the way Claude Code does — the PreToolUse hooks in
`.claude/settings.json` are a Claude Code feature and they do not run here. In
Cursor the boundary is only as good as this rule, so hold it deliberately: when
you are about to run a command in the terminal, that is the moment to dispatch
instead.
